tjp@twg.com (Ted Pederson) writes:
>                                        ... I would like to
>suggest getting rid of the possibility of being teleported and
>paralyzed simultaneously when trying to read a spellbook.  
>
>My Preist had saved his spellbooks until he was level 12,  wisdom 18,
>intelligence 14,  with maximium luck.  He was locked in a room,
>standing on "Elbereth" engraved by a wand of digging.  Upon reading a 
>uncursed spellbook he was simultaneously teleported and paralysed,  and 
>of course I got to hit the spacebar 50-60 times and watch him die at the 
>hands of a few relatively harmless monsters.  And this isn't the first 
>time this has happened. 

I watched the final few moments of this game.  (I work with Ted.)  One thing
he didn't mention is that he did successfully read the spellbook before.  So
he already knew that it wasn't a very expensive spell.

I agree with him whole-heartedly.  If low-level uncursed (or any) spellbooks 
can teleport you *and* paralyze you, a line of sillyness has been crossed.
One should have other options than *having* to bless spellbooks to read them.
Let's get rid of the teleport-paralysis combo, OK?

